{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793379954,"nonce":"i02lLVD6yyBKhc3siV+pG/8+pXg=","message":"Spike: a real Heaps 2.1 app (tests/surface/HeapsProducer.hx) runs under ash --mode hybrid with the SDL3 hlsdl from ash/examples/heaps_base2d, renders s2d to an offscreen texture, and streams damage rectangles through SurfacePump into a PixelSurface; input applied (pointer press echoed). 60 frames at 640x360: first frame 900 KB raw, later frames about 26 KB raw on average (a moving circle), EXIT delivered. Caveats: the app still opens a visible SDL window (not headless); this is the host's GPU, not a guest with software GL (784b568); the readback is capturePixels each frame; pointer injection calls the Interactive's onPush directly, not Heaps' event queue; input latency and sustained fps not measured; ash printed a gc safepoint warning once in the viewer process. Heaps trace output goes to stdout and corrupts the protocol unless redirected, so the shim must redirect haxe.Log.trace first. Run: stage the .hl beside ash/examples/heaps_base2d/bin/*.hdll, set RAYDE_HEAPS_DIR, run SurfaceFeedChecks.","files":null}]}